            <ArticleTitle>Noninvasive diagnosis of left ventricular outflow tract obstruction caused by a porcine mitral prosthesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>698-700</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient developed shortness of breath 8 years after mitral valve replacement with a porcine prosthesis. Doppler echocardiography revealed left ventricular outflow tract obstruction created by a protruding prosthesis.</AbstractText>
